    "title": "Populate Next Right Pointers in Each Node",
    "category": "Trees",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "Given a binary tree, connect every node to its immediate neighbor on the same level using a next pointer. If no such neighbor exists, the next pointer must be set to null.",
    "input": "\u2022 The first line contains an integer N. \u2022 The next N lines describe the binary tree.",
    "output": "\u2022 Print the value of the next pointer for every node in level order.",
    "constraints": "\u2022 0 \u2264 N \u2264 2 \u00d7 10^5________________________________________"
